    "title": "Friends raise funds for family of Batavia man killed in ATV crash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff ,\n5 hours ago\nPhoto via GoFundMe Friends and coworkers are raising money to help the family of Michael Wittmeyer, the 23-year-old Batavia man killed in an ATV accident in Pembroke last Saturday.\nBrian Augello of Rochester, who has worked with Wittmeyer's father for 23 years, organized a GoFundMe campaign to help the family with expenses and any memorial or tribute they may wish to create.\n\"Please help this wonderful family during this unimaginable time,\" Augello wrote on the campaign page.\nWittmeyer died June 20 after the black Yamaha ATV he was riding failed to navigate a bend on Ellinwood Road near 9281 Ellinwood Road. The vehicle left the roadway and struck a tree, ejecting Wittmeyer. Medics attempted life-saving measures, but he was pronounced dead at the scene by the Genesee County Coroner's Office.\nDonations can be made at https://www.gofundme.com/f/support-and-love-for-the-wittmeyer-family .",
    "summary": "Photo via GoFundMe Friends and coworkers are raising money to help the family of Michael Wittmeyer, the 23-year-old Batavia man killed in an ATV accident in Pembroke last Saturday. Brian Augello of Rochester, who has worked with Wittmeyer's father for 23 years, organized a GoFundMe campaign to help the family with expenses and any memorial or tribute they may wish to create. \"Please help this wonderful family during this unimaginable time,\" Augello wrote on the campaign page. The vehicle left the roadway and struck a tree, ejecting Wittmeyer.",
